/*Getting the out of the code snippet

try {
String name = null;
System.out.printf("The length of the string is - %d", name.length());
}
catch (RuntimeException e) {
System.out.printf("Runtime Exception");
}
catch (NullPointerException e) {
System.out.println("Null Pointer
Exception");
}

Output will be a Compilation Error. This is because, from inheritance relationship,
Exception - RuntimeException-NullPointerException. The error will be handled at runtime(compilation)
 and the NullPointer will need not be executed.

